1
00:00:00,340 --> 00:00:02,460
(Amy:)I would. I love cats.

2
00:00:02,460 --> 00:00:03,800
(Amy:)They're the epitome
of indifference.

3
00:00:03,800 --> 00:00:07,620
(Sheldon:)Ah, then you may find
Zazzles a little cloying.

4
00:00:08,690 --> 00:00:10,470
(Leonard:)I saw what you did there.

5
00:00:10,470 --> 00:00:12,560
(Mrs Cooper:)He thinks he's such a smarty pants.

6
00:00:12,560 --> 00:00:13,940
(Mrs Cooper:)He's no different from any man.

7
00:00:13,940 --> 00:00:16,310
(Mrs Cooper:)You tell 'em not to do
something, that's all

8
00:00:16,310 --> 00:00:17,280
(Mrs Cooper:)they want to do.

9
00:00:17,280 --> 00:00:18,780
(Mrs Cooper:)If I hadn't told my brother Stumpy

10
00:00:18,780 --> 00:00:20,760
(Mrs Cooper:)not to clear out the
wood chipper by hand,

11
00:00:20,760 --> 00:00:22,310
(Mrs Cooper:)we'd still be calling him Edward.

12
00:00:23,950 --> 00:00:25,100
(Mrs Cooper:)Now, don't you move.

13
00:00:25,100 --> 00:00:26,700
(Mrs Cooper:)I'll bring over all the food.

14
00:00:26,700 --> 00:00:28,800
(Leonard:)No, no, no, I can do it.

15
00:00:29,940 --> 00:00:32,810
(Mrs Cooper:)Well, isn't that sweet?

16
00:00:39,940 --> 00:00:41,570
(Sheldon:)Thank you, Amy.

17
00:00:41,570 --> 00:00:43,070
(Sheldon:)Here's your cat.

18
00:00:44,160 --> 00:00:45,870
(Sheldon:)And here's your $20.

